export anchor MobileFirstStyle:
    number: 217
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Mobile first
    idea: Designed for one thumb on a phone, with big rounded cards in a single column, progress rings, 48px touch targets and a bottom tab bar with a raised New project button, which becomes a navigation rail and a three column grid of the same cards on a desktop.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f5f4f1, the warm off white behind the cards
        card: #ffffff, cards, the tab bar, the rail and the search pill
        line: #e6e4df, dividers inside cards and above the tab bar
        text: #17171c, titles and body
        muted: #595964, meta, inactive tabs and labels
        indigo: #3b3fc4, the raised New project button, active tab, rings, this week bars and focus
        indigoTint: #ecebfd, the active tab pip and KPI icon tiles
        onTrack: #157a3c, text on a #e2f4e8 pill with a circle and tick
        atRisk: #8f5200, text on a #fcf0dc pill with a triangle and bang
        behind: #b8202e, text on a #fde8ea pill with an octagon and cross, and the overdue card
    type:
        Display text uses ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, system-ui,
        -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif, and body text uses
        system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Noto Sans, Helvetica
        Neue, Arial, sans-serif. The greeting is 30px extra bold rounded,
        KPI values 32px extra bold rounded, section heads 21px, card
        titles 17px bold, body 16px and never smaller in fields, meta 14px
        and tab labels 12px semibold.
    layout:
        On a phone a single column with a 16px gutter. An app bar holds
        the mark and the name Brightwork with a round bell button and the
        avatar at the right. Then the date over a big greeting, a full
        width 52px search pill, and a soft red card with an octagon,
        4 tasks are overdue in bold and a chevron. The KPIs are a two by
        two grid of white tiles, each with a tinted icon tile, a big value
        and a label. A Projects head with See all leads to six stacked
        cards, each with a 56px progress ring showing the percent in its
        centre, the name, the team and tasks, and a divided footer row
        with the due date and days left on the left and a status pill on
        the right. Then a chart card with two week total tiles, last week
        59 and this week 73 up 14, over the bar chart, and an activity card
        with round initials. The tab bar is sticky at the bottom of the
        dashboard and sits at its end, with Home, Projects, a raised 56px
        indigo plus button for New project, Tasks and a More menu that
        opens upward with Team, Reports and Settings. From 900px a 96px
        white rail replaces the tab bar on the left with the mark, the
        raised plus button and stacked icon and label items, Settings at
        the foot. The app bar then holds the greeting, a 380px search, the
        bell and avatar. Content becomes a three column grid with the
        overdue card full width, the KPIs four across, the six project
        cards three across, and the chart card spanning two columns beside
        the activity card.
    spacing: A 16px phone gutter, 12px between cards and 20px between sections. On a desktop a 32px gutter and 20px gaps.
    density: Roomy and touch sized. Every control is at least 44px, tabs are 52px and the raised button 56px.
    corners: 20px cards, 16px tiles and fields, 18px on the raised button, full pills for search, buttons and status.
    borders: Almost none. A 1px line inside project cards and above the tab bar.
    shadows: A faint 0 1px 2px under cards. The raised button has a 0 4px 12px indigo glow and the More menu floats at 0 8px 28px.
    icons:
        22px line icons at stroke 2, inside 56 by 30px pips on tabs and
        36px tinted tiles on KPIs. Status pills carry a circle with a
        tick, a triangle with a bang or an octagon with a cross.
    focus: A 3px indigo outline offset 3px on every control. A focused field also turns its border indigo.
    tone: Short and friendly, such as See all, More, up 14 and The most urgent thing today.
